stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> DRAFT: Routine created from a proposal
    DRAFT --> PENDING_REVIEW: submit_for_review()
    PENDING_REVIEW --> APPROVED: approve()
    PENDING_REVIEW --> REJECTED: reject(observations)
    PENDING_REVIEW --> REPLACED: replace()
    REJECTED --> PENDING_REVIEW: resubmit_for_review()
    APPROVED --> [*]
    REPLACED --> [*]

    note right of DRAFT
        DRAFT is the initial persisted status. A draft must be submitted
        before it can enter the review lifecycle.
    end note

    note right of REJECTED
        An unfavorable review requires non-empty observations (R10).
    end note

    note right of REPLACED
        The replacement keeps a lineage reference to the routine it replaces
        (R11). REPLACED is a domain state; the physical CHECK constraint and
        the E1-08 trigger must be extended before it can be persisted.
    end note

    note right of PENDING_REVIEW
        E1-08 trigger trg_sync_routine_status keeps the persisted status in
        sync with the latest validation and only accepts
        PENDING_REVIEW -> APPROVED/REJECTED. Domain transitions are stricter:
        DRAFT must first be submitted, and only PENDING_REVIEW can be
        approved, rejected or replaced.
    end note
